 "notes": [
  "pres2024 and turnout2022 are exact official district figures: the 2022 and 2024 general elections were run on the 2022 house district plan (400 identical precinct codes and names with the same district prefix in both years; JBER split into JBER No.1/No.2, both HD18). District-level Absentee, Early Voting and Question rows count toward their district.",
  "Statewide numbers are the official certified totals; per-unit sums differ only by the HD99 federal overseas bucket: pres2024 units sum 337776 + HD99 401 (Harris 336, Trump 51, other 14) = 338177; sen_prev units sum 354178 + HD99 409 (Gross 347, Sullivan 52, Howe 10) = 354587; turnout2022 units sum 266943 + HD99 104 = 267047.",
  "sen_prev per unit is an ESTIMATE. The 2020 race was reported on the old 2013-2021 house districts; it was re-allocated to the 2022+ districts. Method: (1) 2020 Statement of Votes Cast per precinct (441 precincts) incl. write-ins; (2) each old district's Absentee, Early Voting and Question votes (56.0% of in-district votes) were spread over that old district's precincts in proportion to each precinct's election-day votes for the same candidate; (3) each 2020 precinct = the Census 2020 voting district (VTD) with the same code (all 441 matched, no fallback needed) was split across new districts by 2020 Census voting-age population (PL 94-171 P0030001) of its blocks, using the Census 2022 SLDL block equivalency file; (4) integers by largest remainder per candidate so per-unit sums are exact. Election-day votes from precincts wholly inside one new district: 32.2%; from 91 precincts split between new districts: 11.8%; old-HD fallback crosswalk: 0%.",
  "Sensitivity of the 2020 estimate: versus a plain old-district-to-new-district voting-age-population crosswalk, the per-district Sullivan-Gross margin differs by a median 2.4 points and at most 19.0 points (new HD34).",
  "turnout2022 = 'Voters Cast' (ballots cast) per house district from the official 2022 Statement of Votes Cast by district, not a governor-race total."
 ],
